            {
                "entry_id": "956777db-8b68-336b-9ddf-af5fe6fe9405",
                "word": "polygraphe",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "00ca21b3-f5ed-4886-9b4e-b6a891ebe332",
                        "entry_id": "956777db-8b68-336b-9ddf-af5fe6fe9405",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "polygraphes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "01025748-7846-38dd-9934-e1ca974a2117",
                        "entry_id": "956777db-8b68-336b-9ddf-af5fe6fe9405",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Appareil électronique qui enregistre plusieurs valeurs physiologiques ; il est parfois utilisé comme détecteur de mensonges."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02ec45d0-e0e4-46b7-8715-121b9de063c3",
                                "sense_id": "01025748-7846-38dd-9934-e1ca974a2117",
                                "text": "Au début des années 1960, un sujet passionnait la presse nationale : fallait-il, oui ou non, introduire le détecteur de mensonges dans la procédure criminelle ? L’opinion publique semblait favorable à l’usage de cet outil, appelé polygraphe, censé permettre, grâce à la mesure des pulsions cardiaques, de la respiration et de la sudation, de confondre n’importe quel suspect."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84fe36eb-6bf6-4ebb-b7bf-4becf34d1758",
                        "source_entry_id": "956777db-8b68-336b-9ddf-af5fe6fe9405",
                        "source_sense_id": "01025748-7846-38dd-9934-e1ca974a2117",
                        "source_sense_description": "Détecteur de mensonge",
                        "target_lang_word": "polygraph",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "polygraph",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4ea04685-4cc8-39de-9676-970db1c81a6b",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A device which measures and records several physiological variables such as blood pressure, heart rate, respiration and skin conductivity while a series of questions is being asked to a subject, in an attempt to detect lies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e3a8d2d-394b-4a10-bf4c-18e472ab8aec",
                                                "sense_id": "4ea04685-4cc8-39de-9676-970db1c81a6b",
                                                "text": "It used to be just a plain office with a chair and some instruments on a table. Then they got the new, fancy polygraph system."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27ad2067-2076-3e7d-9fd6-54e0fc835a1c",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A mechanical instrument for multiplying copies of a writing, resembling multiple pantographs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e2f355d-064b-3574-886b-a1a31c7ef5d3",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A collection of different works, either by one or several authors."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cfbf7f83-9389-3b02-8b06-b3016745bd02",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A group of letters that represent a single phoneme."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "83dd4107-4e74-3558-9853-d4378ae66a18",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any group of letters treated as a single item."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33d1574e-dd49-48cd-975b-408309541a46",
                                                "sense_id": "83dd4107-4e74-3558-9853-d4378ae66a18",
                                                "text": "A polygraph consists of an unspecified number of adjacent letters. A polygraph need not be recognisable as a word in a language but if we are attempting to decipher a message which is expected to be in English and we find the heptagraph MEETING it is much more promising than if we find a heptagraph such as DKRPIGX."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c6988c7d-2817-35ea-9948-2445c9c465e4",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An author who writes on many subjects."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e4cec550-d528-35cd-8fed-cd495bcb33de",
                                        "entry_id": "43e2ba1b-db9c-35ca-8f45-8e00f1610f7a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A multidimensional directed graph."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "polygraph",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6cab752-3f0a-3bec-82d5-82ff6bd0282d",
                                        "entry_id": "ef98ae82-2541-3788-93e4-fc56af44a545",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To administer a polygraph test to."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50bf9f6e-31f9-4414-aa6a-fc21d8ae4918",
                                                "sense_id": "e6cab752-3f0a-3bec-82d5-82ff6bd0282d",
                                                "text": "The FBI polygraphed the suspect but learned nothing because they already knew he was lying."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bf47454d-793d-4e2e-9bab-bc832d1473e1",
                        "source_entry_id": "956777db-8b68-336b-9ddf-af5fe6fe9405",
                        "source_sense_id": "01025748-7846-38dd-9934-e1ca974a2117",
                        "source_sense_description": "Détecteur de mensonge",
                        "target_lang_word": "veelschrijver",
                        "target_lang_code": "nl",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "veelschrijver",
                                "target_lang_code": "nl",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "856964cf-41c2-3d44-a8c0-0f6a52f0c6ef",
                                        "entry_id": "a5709487-b575-371e-ad0c-337d7c51aff6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "iemand die heel veel teksten maakt, soms gebruikt als minachtende benaming voor een auteur die meer kwantiteit dan kwaliteit produceert"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88cede2a-5e39-448b-82d1-13633a130aef",
                                                "sense_id": "856964cf-41c2-3d44-a8c0-0f6a52f0c6ef",
                                                "text": "De Dordtse huisjesmelker en veelschrijver Mustafa Karasahin maakt misbruik van zijn recht door de gemeente Dordrecht honderden brieven per jaar te schrijven. Dat kostte de gemeente al enkele tonnen aan het afhandelen van de brieven."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd48d9a8-bfcd-41d3-9144-4e7cb4ce05ec",
                                                "sense_id": "856964cf-41c2-3d44-a8c0-0f6a52f0c6ef",
                                                "text": "Hij was een veelschrijver. Tot zijn bekendste werken behoort de roman Gateway uit 1977, het verhaal van een ruimtestation dat verborgen is in een asteroïde. Het boek heeft later een computerspel geïnspireerd."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d70cb4b1-c820-40c3-ab9c-0aa93ff64519",
                                                "sense_id": "856964cf-41c2-3d44-a8c0-0f6a52f0c6ef",
                                                "text": "Sir Pratchett was een veelschrijver. Toen hij in 2015 op 66-jarige leeftijd overleed aan de gevolgen van de ziekte van Alzheimer, had hij zeventig boeken geschreven waarvan een slordige zeventig miljoen exemplaren waren verkocht. Vooral zijn licht humoristische fantasy over de Schijfwereld (Discworld) sloegen wereldwijd aan: zijn boeken zijn tot nog toe in 37 talen verschenen. Volgens curator Richard Henry wilde de auteur niet dat na zijn dood iemand anders zijn werk zou afmaken."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70a5fe63-f24c-3e52-886b-01125aa6481a",
                                        "entry_id": "a5709487-b575-371e-ad0c-337d7c51aff6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "instrument waarmee meerdere fysiologische reacties tegelijkertijd kunnen worden geregistreerd"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
